 "decisions": [
  "The trail crosses three chasms on chains of six floating rocks, 13 studs apart; each rock hull is 12 long so the gap between rocks is 1 stud and the hop between walk boxes is 6.04 studs (unverified: no jump test).",
  "A 6 s occupancy limit is far above a walking dwell of 0.81 s per rock; at night a walker sinks 1.2 studs per rock, so the sinking only punishes players who stop.",
  "Chasms are 84 studs along the trail and as wide across as the sector allows (clipped to the boundary); the bible gives no chasm size.",
  "Fissure lips: 24 packed outward from the corridor along both rims, four per rim first and spares to any rim with room (8, 7 and 9 per chasm in the default seed); the bank edge may run 25 studs past a chasm end where the other leg of the trail or the sector boundary leaves room.",
  "Calm stones: one on each bank of each chasm (six), the only rest; the bible gives them no zone radius.",
  "Twelve of the 30 rocks are decoys inside the chasms, off the trail. Thorn spires: 10 rise out of the drop, 20 stand on the banks.",
  "Six of 14 rift shards are flagged night_only (the bible says night-only Rift Shards appear, no count).",
  "Rift gates straddle the trail at both gates with the measured gap (-8.41 to 7.36) containing the corridor with the pivot on the centreline; the gap is 0.52 off centre."
 ],
